{"key": "5de9d3ddf4d6f565d0cdfe76742178be", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "Here are the steps the sources give for a terminal with no connection.\n\n- **Check the chip:** Turn the terminal off and open the back cover. Insert the chip in the slot marked SIM1 or SIM2, with the metal side facing down. Close the cover, turn the terminal on and wait for it to connect to the data network. When it shows a connected network (2G or 3G), it is ready to use. Then run a communication test [2].\n- **Restart:** The way to turn the terminal on and off depends on the model. Depending on the model, you press the green key, press the \".\" key and the yellow key together for 2 seconds, hold the green or red key for 5 seconds, or plug in and unplug the power cable [1].\n- **Unstable signal (error ADQ 1-84):** Press the Function key and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, then select Function 46. Make a test sale [3].\n- **Chip registration error (ADQ 1-87):** Confirm the chip is seated properly. Press Function, enter 25 and enter the Merchant Password. Select Function 46, then Function 90, and make a test sale [4].\n\nThe sources don't say which of these on/off methods applies to model T1988B.\n\nMISSING: on/off method for model T1988B", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011Cghzb8vpdhaMFPv8iDc17", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2866}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2866, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2256, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 688, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 286}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
{"key": "88eba9fba6ad3170beda3efd3819581a", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "A ticket for terminal T1988B (Get Clássica) with the reason \"no connection\" is proposed, but it isn't open yet. Please confirm if you want me to open it (action A-1272cb9b). Per [policy:capabilities], a proposal that isn't confirmed expires after 15 minutes.\n\nThe terminal is offline and has been for 5 hours. Its last contact was 04/11/2026 at 05:48. It connects by chip, and the signal shows \"no signal\".\n\nYou can try these steps from the manual first:\n- **Check the chip:** Turn the terminal off and open the back cover. Put the chip in the SIM1 or SIM2 slot with the metal side down. Close the cover and turn the terminal on. Wait for it to show a connected network (2G or 3G), then run a communication test [sup-duvidas-05].\n- **Restart:** The method depends on the model. Depending on the model, you press the green key, press \".\" and the yellow key together for 2 seconds, hold the green or red key for 5 seconds, or unplug and replug the power cable [sup-operacional-01].\n- **Error ADQ 1-84 (unstable signal):** Press Function and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, select Function 46, then make a test sale [sup-erro-adq-1-84-01].\n- **Error ADQ 1-87 (chip registration):** Check that the chip is seated properly. Press Function, enter 25 and enter the Merchant Password. Select Function 46, then Function 90, and make a test sale [sup-erro-adq-1-87-01].\n\nThe sources don't say which on/off method applies to model T1988B. I can pass this to a human agent if you'd like.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CghzbY9L2ipz7U2QpqDDR", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 771}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 771, "cache_read_input_tokens": 3533, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 551, "out